# claude-ssh allowlist — runtime config for the claude-write deploy channel.
#
# CANONICAL LOCATION ON THE NAS:
#   /mnt/user/appdata/claude-ssh/allowlist.cfg
#
# Lives on the array (mode 644, readable by the constrained SSH user)
# rather than /boot/config. /boot is FAT-mounted with dmask=0077, which
# kernel-forces every directory there to mode 700 regardless of chmod —
# the constrained user could not read the allowlist from /boot. Pre-v10
# installs had the file in /boot/config/plugins/claude-ssh/ and silently
# default-denied all plugin/container writes as a result;
# install-runtime.sh migrates that to the new location on upgrade.
#
# Controls which plugins and containers the SSH user is allowed to write
# into. Both the SSH filter and the privileged writer read this file on
# every invocation; default-deny when empty or malformed.
#
# Format:
#   plugin <name>      Allow claude-write plugin-file writes for
#                      /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/<name>/<rel-path>.
#   container <name>   Allow claude-write appdata-script writes for
#                      /mnt/user/appdata/<name>/scripts/.
#
# Names must match: ^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,63}$  (lowercase, digits, hyphen)
# Comments start with #. Blank lines ignored. Invalid entries dropped silently.

# Plugins you want to deploy assets into.
plugin torrent-handler
plugin claude-ssh

# Containers whose hook scripts you want to deploy.
container sonarr
container radarr
container bazarr
